The crucial change here is checking if the map is an instance of `Collections.UnmodifiableMap` or `Collections.SingletonMap` (or other unmodifiable types) and converting it to a `HashMap`. This ensures that when key-value pairs are added, no exceptions are thrown.

The compilation error you encountered is due to attempting to directly reference `Collections.UnmodifiableMap` and `Collections.SingletonMap`, which are private classes within the `Collections` utility class. Instead, we need to rely on the properties of the map itself to determine if it is immutable.

